                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "587a9d2d-873c-338f-82f6-8ec1f2bcd9b8",
                        "entry_id": "4605e531-6de1-3d7c-b875-d22e16548abb",
                        "glosses": [
                            "past passive perfective participle of пересоли́ть (peresolítʹ)"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "form-of",
                            "participle",
                            "passive",
                            "past",
                            "perfective"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "cb3294d1-2c69-4b00-90ad-9b260d272bc4",
                                "sense_id": "587a9d2d-873c-338f-82f6-8ec1f2bcd9b8",
                                "text": "Все ку́шанья бы́ли пересо́лены, из недожа́ренных цыпля́т сочи́лась кровь и, в дове́ршение всего́, во вре́мя обе́да из рук Пелаге́и сы́пались таре́лки и ножи́, как с похили́вшейся по́лки, но никто́ не сказа́л ей ни сло́ва упрёка, так как все понима́ли состоя́ние её ду́ха.",
                                "translation": "All the dishes were too salt, and blood oozed from the half-raw chickens, and, to cap it all, plates and knives kept dropping out of Pelageya's hands during dinner, as though from a shelf that had given way; but no one said a word of blame to her, as they all understood the state of her feelings.",
                                "english": "All the dishes were too salt, and blood oozed from the half-raw chickens, and, to cap it all, plates and knives kept dropping out of Pelageya's hands during dinner, as though from a shelf that had given way; but no one said a word of blame to her, as they all understood the state of her feelings."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
